**Date:** 28 October 2026 · **Deciders:** support desk · **Replaces:** [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)

## Context

Decision 0001 merges reports on subject alone. [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) shows the cost: reports
about three different problems use the same words ("Date is wrong"), so they landed in one ticket
marked known, with one fix queued for one of them. See [what #4471 hid](/kb/incidents/4471/problems).
Engineering merges separate tickets later; nobody splits merged ones.

## Decision

Two reports are the same issue when they share a cause: the tenant (its locale and booking form)
and the channel, as `causes.ts` reads them. The subject line and the intake tag do not decide it.
A report the desk reads differently from its cause (`desk-notes.json`) gets its own ticket.

## Consequences

- Merging needs the tenant directory, not only the subject. The rule already runs in `causes.ts`.
- Big tickets stay one problem each, so a queued fix closes the whole ticket.
- 0001 is not edited; this record replaces it.

